            "target_entity_instance": "dust AOD",
            "target_entity_type": "Variable",
            "paragraph": "We also compared MODIS DOD climatology with both AERONET observation and DOD retrieved from Cloud-Aerosol Lidar with Orthogonal Polarization (CALIOP; Winker et al., 2004, 2007) aboard the Cloud-Aerosol Lidar and Infrared Pathfinder Satellite Observation (CALIPSO) satellite. AERONET stations provide cloud-screened and quality assured (level 2) coarse-mode aerosol optical depth (COD) at 500 nm, which is processed using the spectral de-convolution algorithm (O'Neill et al., 2003). Only nine sites have long-term COD records during 2003\u20132016, and the climatological mean of MODIS DOD generally compares well with these sites (Fig. S4). CALIOP measures backscattered radiances attenuated by the presence of aerosols and clouds and retrieves corresponding microphysical and optical properties of aerosols. Monthly dust AOD (or DOD) measurements on a 2\u00ba latitude by 5\u00b0 longitude grid are available since June 2006.",
